reconstructd listens on TCP port 7077. The wire format is JSON Lines: each nonempty request line is one JSON object and the daemon emits exactly one JSON object followed by a newline. Success responses contain ok:true; failures contain ok:false and an error string.

A begin request is {"op":"begin","run_id":string,"channels":positive integer,"calibration":1|2|3,"modes":positive integer}. A run accepts frame and correction requests in any order after begin, then exactly one finalize, then query requests. A frame is {"op":"frame","run_id":string,"seq":nonnegative integer,"data":string}. data is base64 of channels signed little-endian int16 values followed by a little-endian CRC-16/CCITT over the value bytes; CRC polynomial is 0x1021 and initial value is 0xffff. Invalid base64, length, sequence, channel payload, or CRC returns BAD_FRAME and increments rejected without storing a frame. A valid duplicate replaces the prior frame and increments duplicate. Corrections are {"op":"correction","run_id":string,"seq":nonnegative integer,"corrections":array of exactly channels finite numeric additive raw ADC values}; malformed corrections return INVALID and do not change state.

The native decoder is /usr/local/libexec/modalcodec. Its binary request is uint32 little-endian calibration, uint16 little-endian channels, uint16 little-endian mode count, and corrected signed little-endian int16 channel values. It emits little-endian float64 coefficients. Revision 1 uses gain 1 and offset 0, revision 2 uses gain 1.25 and offset -3, and revision 3 uses gain .75 and offset 4. Coefficient j is sum over i of ((((i+1)*(j+2)) mod 17)-8)*calibrated[i]/9 plus (j+1)*.125. Corrections are applied in raw-channel space before this decoder conversion. The report retains min(modes, channels) decoder modes.

Frames are ordered by numeric sequence. Missing is the count of integer gaps between the smallest and largest accepted sequence and missing sequences are not observations. The report mean and covariance use only accepted retained observations; covariance is population covariance divided by the number of observations, and is zero for no or one observation. Eigenvalues are descending, eigenvectors are normalized columns, and each vector is sign-oriented so its largest-magnitude component is positive. Tiny negative eigenvalues caused by roundoff may be reported as zero, but substantive negative values must not be hidden.

finalize returns {"ok":true,"report":report} and atomically caches the report. query is valid only after finalize and returns that exact cached report without recomputation or mutation. Reports contain run_id, calibration, counts {accepted,rejected,duplicate,missing}, mean, covariance, eigenvalues, and eigenvectors. Invalid phase, unknown run, duplicate begin, malformed JSON, and malformed requests return an error and never mutate run state. Multiple independent run IDs may share one connection.
